        "id": "tool:answer-the-calendar-page-route",
        "label": "Answer the calendar page routes",
        "status": "active",
        "job": "Answer the page's calendar routes (GET /work/api/calendar, GET and POST /work/api/calendar/tasks, and the task proposal and date-shift routes) from the calendar rows handed in",
        "description": "The page's calendar routes, run by the engine for the page's account (workshop-routes): the request's { path, method, query, body, browser, records } in, { status, body, keep } out. Each read is answered by old trillion's own calendar owner (src/native-calendar-owner.mjs calendar:request) over the calendar rows the caller hands in as `records` ([{id, type, value}]); this run reads no store of its own. A read may answer in `keep` the starting calendar list definitions it finds missing, rows for the caller to keep where the person keeps them, conditional on the rows it read. GET /calendar reads every source; the person's tasks are read here, and a source only another route or a connected calendar tool can read is said unread in the calendar's own words. A POST to the task, proposal or date-shift routes answers 405: keeping those is workflow:keep-my-calendar-tasks-and-proposals. /calendar/actions and /calendar/availability are not answered here (404).",
        "input_schema": {
          "type": "object",
          "required": [
            "path",
            "method"
          ],
          "properties": {
            "path": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "The route after /work/api (/calendar, /calendar/tasks, ...)"
            },
            "method": {
              "type": "string",
              "enum": [
                "GET",
                "POST"
              ]
            },
            "query": {
              "type": "object"
            },
            "body": {},
            "browser": {
              "type": "object"
            },
            "records": {
              "type": "array",
              "maxItems": 5000,
              "description": "The calendar rows this run reads, read by the caller from the person's own store and handed in: [{id, type, value}] of the kinds the lists keep for the calendar (list:calendar-tasks and its record:calendar-task rows, the calendar task lists and their day hours and working hours, the lists' entity, open-mark, trash, tombstone, proposal, heat, view, filter and snapshot rows named by their ids, and workspace-preference:calendar-selections). What is not given is not there."
            }
          }
        },
        "output_schema": {
          "type": "object",
          "required": [
